I think a stiff / non-stiff solver option would be very useful as well. Using a stiff solver is costly and should be avoided if not needed. If cvode will be used as backend, this means using the adams & functional option when initializing (and one must not setup a dense solver).

Sebastian

BTW: Assuming that cvode will be integrated into Stan, then I think the standard integrate_ode should make use of the non-stiff solver of cvode. This will give users a much improved ODE solver at hand and will avoid requests from many frustrated users using the boost solver which tends to lock up.

The cvode branch from Michael looks great! Looking forward to the development of this feature.

