> Or do you mean streaming where you accumulate means and covariances?
> It's not possible to compute streaming medians without storing at
> least half of what would be in that .csv file in memory or somewhere.
> 95% intervals could be done storing 5% of the data in memory and so on

Median’s require just two samples — you throw away everything other
than the central two values, which can be done streaming.  Then interpolate
the two central values however you like to give the median estimator.

