Subject: Re: [stan-dev] value_of vs value_of_rec?
Message-ID: <pALkQ1NpRvs.Z2wJ4QdZDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <pALkQ1NpRvs.gfT_slZVDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
References: <pALkQ1NpRvs.gfT_slZVDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/pALkQ1NpRvs/m/Z2wJ4QdZDwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

value_of_rec returns the underlying double value, no matter the autodiff order (fvar<var> or fvar<fvar<var> >) whereas value_of will return the nested var or fvar.

So, value_of(fvar<var> x) returns x.val_ whereas value_of_rec(fvar<var> x) returns x.val_.val()

Rob

