Subject: Re: [stan-dev] ADIC: auto diff for c sources?
Message-ID: <gcGnzrcYwXs.dw0akMm4DwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <gcGnzrcYwXs.85soIIuTDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
References: <gcGnzrcYwXs.XEL7cgKTDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com> <gcGnzrcYwXs.85soIIuTDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/gcGnzrcYwXs/m/dw0akMm4DwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

We've thought about code generation off and on.  It's what
Theano (Python) does.

The problem is conditionals and branching.  If we could get
rid of all of those, code generation is a no-brainer.  But if
we'd done that, we woudn't have many of our matrix algorithms
and would've taken a lot longer to get ODEs out, etc.

We may still think about more in the future if we could
limit Stan's language's expressiveness.

- Bob

