From u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com  Tue Sep 29 19:04:49 2015
From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2015 19:04:49 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-dev] ADIC: auto diff for c sources?
Message-ID: <gcGnzrcYwXs.Z-LJ1-i4DwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <gcGnzrcYwXs.85soIIuTDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
References: <gcGnzrcYwXs.XEL7cgKTDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com> <gcGnzrcYwXs.85soIIuTDwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/gcGnzrcYwXs/m/Z-LJ1-i4DwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

clad is just forward mode, which isn't so useful.  Stan's C++
templates do efficient forward mode, so you don't need to code
generate (or maybe I should say is that the template system gives
you all you need to code generate).

We need reverse mode for efficient gradients O(1) relative to
function evaluation rather than O(N) in forward mode.

- Bob

